{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The work of Elohim they are.</b> As it sounds — He in His glory made them. Another interpretation: as a person says to his friend, 'All of So-and-so's affairs are in such-and-such a trade' — so, all the delights of the Holy One, blessed be He, are in the Torah." "<b>Graven.</b> חָרַת and חָרַט are one — both are a term of engraving; אנטלי״יר בְּלַעַז."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French entaillier, 'to engrave/carve'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:10.126615477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}